[?2004l[?2004h> # MLService Deployment Fix
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Problem
[?2004l[?2004h> The service was failing with "No module named 'tokenizers'" when run with `python -m mlservice` from within the `/home/user/mlservice` directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Cause
[?2004l[?2004h> When running `python -m mlservice` from inside the mlservice directory itself, Python's module resolution cannot properly import the mlservice package. The package needs to be run from its parent directory (`/home/user`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Solution
[?2004l[?2004h> Use the provided `start_service.sh` script instead of running `python -m mlservice` directly.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For Production Deployment
[?2004l[?2004h> Replace:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> cd /home/user/mlservice
[?2004l[?2004h> source .venv/bin/activate
[?2004l[?2004h> python -m mlservice
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> With:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> cd /home/user/mlservice
[?2004l[?2004h> ./start_service.sh
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Or simply:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> /home/user/mlservice/start_service.sh
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The script handles venv activation and ensures the service runs from the correct directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> The service now successfully imports tokenizers and all other dependencies.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004huser@017c47f8dc78:~/mlservice$ cat DEPLOYMENT_FIX.md
[?2004l# MLService Deployment Fix

## Problem
The service was failing with "No module named 'tokenizers'" when run with `python -m mlservice` from within the `/home/user/mlservice` directory.

## Root Cause
When running `python -m mlservice` from inside the mlservice directory itself, Python's module resolution cannot properly import the mlservice package. The package needs to be run from its parent directory (`/home/user`).

## Solution
Use the provided `start_service.sh` script instead of running `python -m mlservice` directly.

### For Production Deployment
Replace:
```bash
cd /home/user/mlservice
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m mlservice
```

With:
```bash
cd /home/user/mlservice
./start_service.sh
```

Or simply:
```bash
/home/user/mlservice/start_service.sh
```

The script handles venv activation and ensures the service runs from the correct directory.

## Verification
The service now successfully imports tokenizers and all other dependencies.
